--- a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-platform-mt6991-adsp
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-platform-mt6991-adsp
@@ -1,13 +1,13 @@
 What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/.../prepare_boot_records
 Date:		November 2026
 Description:
-		Writing 1 prepares the MT6991 audio DSP core's L2 boot records.
-		The kernel uses the bootloader's verified shared memory range.
-		It checks the core's stall bit with its RX channel powered, writes
-		the MPU record and (on core A) the inter-core record, then reads
-		the records back before releasing the runtime power reference.
-		An active core returns EBUSY, a missing allocation returns ENODATA,
-		an inaccessible control register returns ENXIO, and a failed L2
-		readback returns EIO. Repeating a successful request
-		while the core is stalled writes the same records. Retention across
-		a later power transition is platform dependent.
+		On Turner, writing 1 returns EOPNOTSUPP. The MT6991 platform
+		descriptor in the stock firmware does not select the v1 MPU
+		and inter-core record initialization sequence.
+
+What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/.../boot_records_match
+Date:		November 2026
+Description:
+		Read-only diagnostic comparison of the legacy v1 L2 record
+		locations with the current shared memory layout. A zero is
+		normal on Turner and is not a DSP boot failure indication.
